an outline is a tree. one idea per node, ordered top-down: what it is,
what it promises, how it works, where it stands.

on disk the tree is the outline. on a page — where `general/medium`
picks one — every node folds, and the reader opens all, none, or where
they are.

the index is derived — ls on disk, a script on a page. never typed.

the test: delete a node. any hand edit elsewhere means the outline was
written, not derived.

